# Cerise: real BoringSSL "crypto" (libcrypto) library, vendored to replace a
# previously-undisclosed compatibility stub (src/cerise/stubs/bssl-crypto — a fake
# Sha256 backed by pure-Rust sha2, never registered in the allowlist). Found
# and corrected during Fxfs Phase 1 (fuchsia-merkle needs real bssl-crypto).
#
# Source: fuchsia.googlesource.com/third_party/boringssl, submodule commit
# e056f59c7dfdcf891af03bc7900c946ac485c78f (the exact commit pinned by this
# repo's fuchsia.git tree at 0f3c21bc890c06e8549431abf9d333fbc581937d).
# srcs/hdrs lists are transcribed verbatim from that pin's own
# third_party/boringssl/BUILD.generated.gni (crypto_sources/crypto_headers),
# filtered to the x86_64 Linux assembly variants (crypto_sources_asm entries
# matching "x86_64" and "linux" — GN normally does this filtering via a
# per-toolchain sources-assignment-filter; Bazel has no equivalent so it's
# done explicitly here). NOT vendoring ssl/ or pki/ — bssl-crypto.no-ssl (what
# fuchsia-merkle actually depends on) only needs libcrypto, not libssl/TLS.
